Message-ID: <rfc-eml-001@ailang.sunholo.com>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8

Team,

I'd like to propose adding email parsing (EML and MBOX formats) to
AILANG Parse. Here's the rationale:

1. Email is a common document format that agents need to process
2. EML files contain rich structure: headers, MIME parts, attachments
3. MBOX files bundle multiple messages (useful for archival analysis)
4. The RFC 5322 + MIME specs are well-defined and deterministic

Proposed Block mapping:
  - Email headers -> Text blocks (type: email-header)
  - Plain text body -> Text block
  - HTML body -> parsed via existing HTML parser
  - Attachments -> Text blocks (type: attachment) with metadata
  - MBOX messages -> Section blocks wrapping individual emails

Implementation estimate: ~300 lines of AILANG in eml_parser.ail.

No AI needed — this is fully deterministic.

Thoughts?

Mark

