Great work on the test coverage. One more edge case to consider:

Japanese email clients often use ISO-2022-JP encoding. Example:

  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=ISO-2022-JP

This uses escape sequences to switch between ASCII and JIS X 0208.
Not critical for v1 but worth noting for the backlog.

Also, consider adding a sample with:
  - Multiple To/CC recipients
  - Reply-To different from From
  - X-* custom headers (common in ticketing systems)

Otherwise LGTM. Ship it!

Taro Yamada
